sed "s/^X//" >'README' <<'END_OF_FILE'
XThis "Read Me" concerns patch file Patch01 which upgrades Dinkum
XVersion 2.12 to Version 2.13 .
X
XPaul Russell <paulr@syma.sussex.ac.uk> informed me that Dinkum was not
Xportable to Apple MacIntosh computers.  I am most grateful to Paul for
Xhis providing me with the necessary modifications for Dinkum's source
Xcode to compile in the MacIntosh and for writing the enclosed BinHex
Xfile which produces the necessary C makefile.  The file "BinHex.1" is
Xonly for MacIntosh users and just takes up disk space in any other
Xenvironment.
X
XFred Smith <fredex%fcshome@merk.merk.com> informed me that Dinkum would
Xnot compile on some versions of the Coherent operating system and under
Xsome flavors of Gcc.  I am thankful to Fred for pointing out to me some
Xbad coding technique (not really bugs) in Version 2.12 which was limiting
Xportability.  Look inside "make.unx" and you'll see the lines that need
Xto be changed if you wish to compile under Coherent or some of the odd
Xball flavors of Gcc.  
X
XThe patch file Patch01 incorporates the changes suggested by Paul
XRussell and Fred Smith.  Also included are some very minor typographical
Xerrors which I discovered in Dinkum (no real logic bugs).  If Dinkum
XVersion 2.12 functions correctly in your environment then this patch
Xwill have only a very minor effect and may not be worth the trouble
Xto install.  However if you're a Mac user or Dinkum does not compile on
Xyour box then this maybe the patch for you.
X
X                          Gary A. Allen, Jr.
END_OF_FILE
